module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.MapDomain
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Congruence.Hom
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Span
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Maps

/-!
# Kernel of a monoid-algebra quotient induced by a congruence

Source: Mathlib/GroupTheory/Congruence/Hom.lean, `AddCon.mk'_ker` and `AddCon.lift`
(supporting quotient facts; the kernel formula itself is proved in the node)
(blueprint: lem-trf-congruence-polynomial-kernel).

For an additive congruence `c` on a commutative monoid `M` and a commutative ring `A`, the
kernel of `A[M] → A[c.Quotient]` is spanned by the differences of congruent basis monomials,
and by the differences coming from a generating set when `c = addConGen S`.
-/

universe u v

@[expose] public section

open scoped AddMonoidAlgebra

/--
Source: Mathlib/GroupTheory/Congruence/Hom.lean, `AddCon.mk'_ker`
(blueprint: lem-trf-congruence-polynomial-kernel).

Let `M` be an additive commutative monoid, `c : AddCon M`, and `A` a commutative
ring. The kernel of the additive monoid-algebra map induced by `c.mk'` is the
ideal generated by differences of basis monomials indexed by `c`-equivalent
terms. If `c = addConGen S`, the same kernel is generated by the differences
coming from `S`. The postponed proof follows the node's seven steps: (1) every
listed difference maps to zero, giving one inclusion; (2) group a finite
support by quotient classes and record the coefficient sums; (3) choose one
representative in each nonempty class and rewrite each class as differences;
(4) conclude the first kernel equality, including empty support; (5) for
`c = addConGen S`, define the relation detected by the ideal generated by
`S` and prove it is an additive congruence; (6) minimality of `addConGen S`
gives the reverse inclusion of congruences; (7) the two ideal inclusions give
the second kernel equality. No cancellativity of `M` is used.
-/
theorem congruence_polynomial_kernel
    {M : Type u} {A : Type v} [AddCommMonoid M] [CommRing A] (c : AddCon M) :
    RingHom.ker (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom A c.mk') =
        Ideal.span
          {x : AddMonoidAlgebra A M |
            ∃ u w : M, c u w ∧
              x = AddMonoidAlgebra.of' A M u - AddMonoidAlgebra.of' A M w} ∧
      ∀ S : Set (M × M), c = addConGen (fun u w => (u, w) ∈ S) →
        RingHom.ker (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom A c.mk') =
          Ideal.span
            {x : AddMonoidAlgebra A M |
              ∃ p : M × M, p ∈ S ∧
                x = AddMonoidAlgebra.of' A M p.1 - AddMonoidAlgebra.of' A M p.2} := by
  sorry
